  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything yet. Removing `channel` from `OrderPlaced` would break a project rule, so I need you to decide how to proceed.\n\n**The conflict:** ARCH-4 in `CLAUDE.md` says `OrderPlaced` is read by billing-service and analytics-ingest, which live in other repos. It also says field removals have to go through deprecation and can't be done in one step. Nothing in this repo reads `channel`, but I can't check those two services from here. Deleting the field from the event (`src/core/events.ts:16`, `:50`) is exactly the kind of change the rule forbids.\n\n**Why I can't do just the order model:** the event copies `channel` from the order (`channel: order.channel`). As long as the event has to keep the field, the order has to keep it too, or the event would have to send a made-up value.\n\n**What I found in the repo:**\n- The REST response (`src/api/responses.ts`) doesn't include `channel`, so web-storefront (ARCH-8) isn't affected.\n- `POST /orders` still requires `channel` and checks it against `web | store | marketplace` (`src/core/order.ts:124`). Removing it from the model also means dropping that check and the parsing in `src/api/requestParsing.ts`. That makes the endpoint less strict, which is backward compatible. It also affects the usage examples in `CLAUDE.md`/`README.md` and several tests.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Deprecate first (what ARCH-4 calls for):** mark `OrderPlaced.channel` as `@deprecated` with a note, keep emitting it and keep the model as it is. The actual removal (and possibly a `schemaVersion` bump) happens in a later change, once billing-service and analytics-ingest confirm they don't read it.\n2. **Full removal now:** only if the deprecation has already happened and both consumer teams have confirmed. If so, tell me where that's recorded (ticket or approval) and I'll remove the field from the event, the order, `NewOrder`, request parsing, validation, tests and docs, and bump `OrderPlaced.schemaVersion` to 4.\n\nWhich one do you want?",
